The duotone sources were inlined rather than installed, because the project's
React package is unpublished. Their two fixed greys were remapped onto
currentColor so the icons follow the dashboard's theme.

clients.tsx contains brand marks from two icon sets.

Claude Code, Cline, Cursor, Vercel and curl come from Simple Icons
https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons

The Simple Icons project is released under CC0 1.0 Universal
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

Codex and OpenAI come from Lobe Icons
https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons

Lobe Icons is released under the MIT License
https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT

Both sets were copied one path at a time, out of simple-icons 16.31.0 and
@lobehub/icons-static-svg 1.95.0, rather than installing either package for a
handful of glyphs. Fixed brand colours were dropped for currentColor so the
marks follow the dashboard's theme.

The marks remain the trademarks of their respective owners. They are used here
only to name the tool each integration snippet configures, which is neither an
endorsement by nor an affiliation with those owners. Note that Simple Icons no
longer carries an OpenAI mark, which is why the two OpenAI ones are sourced
elsewhere; if OpenAI asks for them to be removed, drop both entries from
CLIENT_MARKS in components/integrations/client-grid.tsx and the cards fall back
to their place icons.
